f="c-11" decimals="3" name="us-gaap:OperatingLeaseWeightedAverageDiscountRatePercent" scale="-2" id="f-2680">5.1</ix:nonFraction>%).</span></div></div></div></ix:continuation><div style="height:36pt;position:relative;width:100%"><div style="bottom:0;position:absolute;width:100%"><div style="text-align:center"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">79</span></div></div></div><div id="i212bfd6c10fa44bfb2860b18813e3381_268"></div><hr style="page-break-after:always"/><div style="min-height:36pt;width:100%"><div style="margin-bottom:5pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"><a style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;text-decoration:none" href="#i212bfd6c10fa44bfb2860b18813e3381_7">Table of Contents</a> &#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span></div></div><div style="width:100.000%"><div style="display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;width:48.412%"><ix:continuation id="f-2458-13" continuedAt="f-2458-14"><div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">PPAs and Fuel Contracts</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Non-Lease PPAs</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"> </span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">&#8212;</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"> NSP-Minnesota, PSCo and SPS have entered into PPAs with other utilities and energy suppliers for purchased power to meet system load and energy requirements, operating reserve obligations and as part of wholesale and commodity trading activities. In general, these agreements provide for energy payments, based on actual energy delivered, and may also include capacity payments. Certain non-lease PPAs with various expiration dates through 2040, contain minimum energy purchase commitments. Total energy payments on those contracts were $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-948" decimals="-6" name="us-gaap:UtilitiesOperatingExpensePurchasedPowerUnderLongTermContracts" scale="6" id="f-2681">111</ix:nonFraction> million, $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-949" decimals="-6" name="us-gaap:UtilitiesOperatingExpensePurchasedPowerUnderLongTermContracts" scale="6" id="f-2682">212</ix:nonFraction> million and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-950" decimals="-6" name="us-gaap:UtilitiesOperatingExpensePurchasedPowerUnderLongTermContracts" scale="6" id="f-2683">214</ix:nonFraction> million in 2025, 2024 and 2023, respectively.</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Included in electric fuel and purchased power expenses for PPAs accounted for as executory contracts were payments for capacity of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-951" decimals="-6" name="us-gaap:UtilitiesOperatingExpensePurchasedPowerUnderLongTermContracts" scale="6" id="f-2684">49</ix:nonFraction> million, $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-952" decimals="-6" name="us-gaap:UtilitiesOperatingExpensePurchasedPowerUnderLongTermContracts" scale="6" id="f-2685">81</ix:nonFraction> million and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-953" decimals="-6" name="us-gaap:UtilitiesOperatingExpensePurchasedPowerUnderLongTermContracts" scale="6" id="f-2686">77</ix:nonFraction> million in 2025, 2024 and